      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could say: \n\n  When a service authenticates for a token,\n\nWe could also add a definition to service tokens, so that it\u0027s apparent that there really isn\u0027t anything special about \"service\" tokens and that they really are just tokens associated to users with a special name.\n\nI think a lot of people trip when they see the term \"service token\" because they expect it to be difference contractually from any other token keystone issues.",
